Trust-reset integration front: do not call a lane accepted unless the current proof includes Chrome/DevTools-visible browser behavior. Pre-reset supporting proof remains useful but is not enough by itself. [[BMH Institute]] `course.completed`→[[Sandra]] has fresh Chrome/DevTools revalidation after Sandra #227/#228 and BMH Institute #81: `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-current.*` visibly shows `Lesson complete`, and separate outcome confirmation shows Sandra `institute_course_outcomes.id=61592447-b33d-489c-a230-d513435ef6b7` with webhook event `15e56f40-31b8-4d48-901e-942bdf0bbd8f` processed/signature verified. [[Closer Lab]] practice outcome→[[Sandra]] now has fresh Chrome/DevTools member recording revalidation: `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-member-recording.*` visibly shows attempt `72ad25d8-1b09-4ef9-a278-82113c12ce75`, `100%`, transcript, and rubric `MET 5 / 5`; separate support file `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-sandra-outcome-support.json` ties the same attempt to Sandra `closer_practice_outcomes.id=90aaae3d-1053-4021-b9e1-a6e50b8a08f8`. [[Jitter]]→[[Sandra]] writeback remains supported by deployed production executor/API plus Sandra production DB proof after Jitter #145, Sandra #224, and Jitter #146, and a controlled Chrome `/dialer` proof succeeded after production was pinned to canonical `jitter-test` (`ypgntjjrrutjsratdwmk`). That proof is still not sufficient for acceptance because it depended on a local scoped worker. Current gap: a real worker path must back the final Chrome proof so dialing continues without the local helper and without warning banners, duplicate operations, or queue-time spikes.

